  </table></ix:nonNumeric>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">Book values approximate to fair value at 31 December 2025, 2024 and
2023.</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">Promissory note</p>

<p style="font: bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-weight: normal">In December 2024 the Company issued
a Promissory Note to C/M Capital Master Fund, LP in the aggregate principal amount of $600,000 at a 10% original issue discount. The Note
is an unsecured obligation of the Company and bears interest at an annual rate of 5%, which may be increased under certain circumstances,
and has a maturity date of one year from the Issuance Date. The Note includes a monthly repayment schedule, with the entire principal
amount of the Note, plus accrued and unpaid interest, due and payable by the Company on the date that is twelve months from the Issuance
Date.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-weight: normal">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-weight: normal"></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-weight: normal">The Company received $540,000 pursuant
to the Promissory Note on 24 December 2024. The note was repaid in full during 2025.</span></p>

<ix:exclude><p id="xdx_235_zZhxKrVFldbg" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: left"><b>&#160;</b></p></ix:exclude>

